rows.en:
Just then, a single ray of morning sun shone in.
The light fell on her face...
And then, for an instant, her face stirred and rippled.{p}

The clatter of the mask hitting the floor brought me back to my senses.
By the time the mask had fallen and rocked to a stop, she was already gone.
She had vanished along with the butterflies.{p}

Had I seen an illusion, or had I been dreaming...?
Then I noticed a single butterfly fluttering around me, as if reluctant to leave.
The morning sun had already fully risen.{p}

"Uh, waaaaaaaaah☆"
My voice rang out through the old school building.
When my voice, echoing through the building, finally died away, a silence that seemed eternal returned.{p}

She looked up and gazed all around the sky.
As if she were someone who had forgotten to look at the sky for years...
I couldn't see her face behind the mask, but that was how it felt to me.{p}

...At that moment.
Her face suddenly began to crumble.
Like wax running in the heat, her face melted and flowed away.{p}

That's right.
There's no way I can be saved.
But you know, I'm not all alone anymore...{p}

"Iwashita, please..."
Had I lost my mind?
Answering a question like that.{p}

Iwashita... the one who had once tried to kill me.
Maybe I felt guilty toward Uchiyama.
Maybe that was why I chose Iwashita.{p}
